%S A123439 1,2,4,11,33,94,278,841,2613,8314,26822,87819,290479,970506,3268856,
%T A123439 11090831,37866395
%N A123439 Number of P_4-lite perfect graphs on n nodes.
%C A123439 A graph is P_4-lite if every induced subgraph on at most 6 vertices either contains at most two induced P_4 (paths on 4 vertices) or is the 3-sun graph or its complement. Equivalently, the graph is C_5-free and P_4-tidy. Every P_4-lite graph is brittle and hence perfect, and the class is closed under induced subgraphs. - _Meghanto Majumder_, Oct 07 2026
%H A123439 S. Hougardy, <a href="http://www.or.uni-bonn.de/~hougardy/">Home Page</a>
